# An unqualified data cardinality, and a functional data property, both used.
# Before 0.2.0 they were labelled as their object twins (ObjectMaxCardinality,
# FunctionalObjectProperty). They are data, and labelled so: omissions
# DataMaxCardinality and a DataAxiom. INCONCLUSIVE (exit 2).

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class .
:A rdfs:subClassOf :B .
:dp a owl:DatatypeProperty , owl:FunctionalProperty .
:A rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :dp ; owl:maxCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ] .
